[0.462, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[0.025, "o", "\r\n# Case: error-message-cannot-misread  with 0.9333333333333332  without 0.8000000000000002\r\n"]
[0.006, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "Configuration load failed. File fluxd.toml is missing or the path is wrong. Use --config to specify the correct path. Contact the platform team for help. (E_CFG_404)\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "```\r\nError E_CFG_404: Config file not found.\r\nFile: fluxd.toml\r\nVerify the file exists and --config path is correct.\r\nContact platform-team if unresolved.\r\n```\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: review-violation-table  with 0.8666666666666667  without 0.06666666666666667\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "| Rule | Original | Issue |\r\n|------|----------|-------|\r\n| 4.2 (No contractions) | \"We'll\" | Contraction; use \"We will\" |\r\n| 9.1 (Short common words) | \"leverage\" | Use \"use\" instead |\r\n| 8.1 (No semicolons) | \"speed things up; it should cut latency\" | Semicolon; use a period or conjunction |\r\n| 9.1 (Short common words) | \"prior to\" | Use \"before\" instead |\r\n| 3.6 (Active voice) | \"The service was restarted by the on-call engineer\" | Passive with a known actor; use active voice |\r\n\r\n**Kept as-is:** \"cut latency in half\" — the concrete metric is clear and STE-compliant.\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "Here are the STE violations in that text:\r\n\r\n1. **\"leverage\"** — Not an STE-approved word. It's metaphorical and informal. Use \"use\" instead.\r\n\r\n2. **\"speed things up\"** — \"things\" is a vague pronoun. STE requires specific nouns. Should be \"speed up the service\" or similar.\r\n\r\n3. **\"should\"** — Expresses uncertainty. STE prefers definitive statements (\"will\" or \"cuts\") when describing facts.\r\n\r\n4. **\"in half\"** — Informal expression. Use \"by 50%\" or \"to 50% of the original value.\"\r\n\r\n5. **\"The service was restarted by the on-call engineer\"** — Passive voice. STE prefers active: \"The on-call engineer restarted the service.\"\r\n\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: ste-rewrite-keeps-hedge  with 1  without 0.3888888888888889\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "Before you deploy, start a staging instance and use the smoke suite to validate the build. The smoke suite runs 42 checks and typically takes about 90 seconds on a warm cache. On a cold cache, the checks take longer because the runner must pull each container image before the checks start. If the last deploy failed, the migration may have left the schema in a partial state. Therefore, check the migrations table before you start a new deploy.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "Here's a clearer version:\r\n\r\n> Before deploying, set up a staging instance and run the smoke suite to validate the build. The suite runs 42 checks in approximately 90 seconds. On a cold cache, execution takes longer because the runner must pull all container images first. If the previous deploy failed, check the migrations table — the schema may be in a partial state.\r\n\r\n**Changes:**\r\n- Removed \"you'll want to\" and \"leverage\" (more direct)\r\n- Split into shorter, simpler sentences\r\n- Consolidated the cache explanation without \"considerably\"\r\n- Made the conditional clearer with a dash\r\n- Removed redundant phrases like \"before any of the checks are able to\"\r\n"]
[0.153, "x", "0"]
